<rss version="2.0" xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/" xmlns:atom="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><channel><title>Hacker News: Front Page</title><link>https://news.ycombinator.com/</link><description>Hacker News RSS</description><docs>https://hnrss.org/</docs><generator>hnrss v2.1.1</generator><lastBuildDate>Mon, 02 Nov 2026 16:59:04 +0000</lastBuildDate><atom:link href="https://hnrss.org/frontpage" rel="self" type="application/rss+xml"></atom:link><item><title><![CDATA[Show HN: Warsaw in voxels – an interactive 3D map of the city centre]]></title><description><![CDATA[
<p>Explore central Warsaw in voxels - slightly inspired by Minecraft, and MagicaVoxel. 
You can change the date, time of day and weather, explore the city, or click on a pedestrian to control them (here a bit of inspiration from Dungeon Keeper).<p>Works best on desktop, but I tried to make it usable on mobile too. The initial load can take a while. It's based on several open datasets, including:<p>- OpenStreetMap (<a href="https://www.openstreetmap.org/#map=6/52.02/19.14" rel="nofollow">https://www.openstreetmap.org/#map=6/52.02/19.14</a>) - buildings, streets, sidewalks, tram tracks, etc<p>- GUGiK / Geoportal (<a href="https://www.geoportal.gov.pl/" rel="nofollow">https://www.geoportal.gov.pl/</a>) - LiDAR for building heights and trees, aerial imagery for colours<p>- Warsaw's city tree database (<a href="https://mapa.um.warszawa.pl/" rel="nofollow">https://mapa.um.warszawa.pl/</a>) - individual tree species, used for seasonal foliage<p>Open-source (<a href="https://github.com/stared/warsaw-vibe-voxel" rel="nofollow">https://github.com/stared/warsaw-vibe-voxel</a>), so feel invited to (re)use it as you wish!</p>
